WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.290
 They'll beat a
tattoo a quarter to two

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.700
with a rat a tat tat
a tat tat a to too.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.380
And the dragons will come when
they sound the drum in a minute

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.715
or two til two today, in
a minute or two til two.

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:10.990
[JAZZ MUSIC]

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:11.590
Hi.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:13.090
Welcome to my class.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.940
A voice-over booth can get
a little claustrophobic.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.470
So how about we do this?

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.150
What better way to
learn about voice

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.760
acting than from an
animated character?

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:28.740
I'm going to tell you a little
story about a girl from Ohio.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.290
The girl got a job
at a radio station

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.920
where she saw that you could
make a living with your voice.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.380
So she worked her way up
and eventually did voices

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.850
for hit cartoons.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.520
It took me getting
cast on "The Simpsons"

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.960
that I realized that I excelled
in doing quirky tomboys.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.210
All right!

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.810
In this class, I'll teach you
everything about voice acting--

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.700
how to develop your characters.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.940
This is just a little character
that I can use as our example.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.670
One of the things
that you can do

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:02.110
is to change the pitch
of your character.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:05.220
I can make him a little
bit lower like this.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.830
Or I can lift him way
up high like this.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.920
Performance tips and how to
start out in the industry.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.780
Nobody knows what you look like.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.190
They don't know how old you are.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.660
They don't know
anything about you.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.310
It's just your voice.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.450
So anybody can do it.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:22.200
And I'll demonstrate how
I bring animation to life

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.190
by voicing several original
characters from a show we

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:29.370
made called "No Effort Girl."

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.070
I didn't ask to be born
with super strength, X-ray

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.622
vision, and the ability to fly.

00:01:33.622 --> 00:01:34.680
Ugh.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.320
You'll learn how to distinguish
your characters so they

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.460
take on a life of their own.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.580
So let's get started.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.310
I'm Nancy Cartwright,
and this is my--

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.410
Wait, what are you doing?

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.120
I'm doing the MasterClass line.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.470
But I'm the real Nancy.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:50.800
I'll do it.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.050
I'm Nancy Cartwright.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.520
I'm Nancy Cartwright.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.070
And this is my MasterClass.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.620
[JAZZ MUSIC]

